(* A LOCAL FUNCTION WHOSE PARAMETER LIST IS NOT GLUED TO ITS NAME.
   `LocalDecl.rats:75` is `Id (w StaticParams)? w ValParam` and `w` is
   `Whitespace*`, so `g (x: ZZ32): ZZ32 = e` is ONE declaration. Requiring the
   parenthesis to be glued read the SPELLING and not the grammar, and this
   spelling died in the PARSER at the `:` with `expected )`.

   `ProjectFortress/tests/funny.fss:29` is the corpus file that writes it, and
   it is the only one -- which is the point: the local-function bucket is 39
   and 39 is now a TRUE ceiling rather than a glued-spelling one. *)

run(): () = do
    g (x: ZZ32): ZZ32 = x + 1
    println(g(4))
end
